Package signing trust anchors (§6.11)
=====================================

Public keys that verify application packages and OS upgrades live in this
directory, on the read-only root filesystem:

    /usr/local/share/auditorium/trusted-keys/

Any *.pub file here can verify a package. Two properties are load-bearing:

  1. This directory is never read through a path under /opt/auditorium,
     because that resolves into /data/app/current — an update package could
     then ship its own key and self-authorise every later update. The anchors
     sit outside anything an update can write.

  2. It is a directory, not a file, so keys can be rotated: replacing the
     anchor needs an OS upgrade, which needs a valid signature from the key
     being replaced. Holding two keys at once breaks that circularity. The
     rollover procedure and the key-loss recovery path are in §14.1 and, step
     by step, in docs/build/packages.md.

The file format
---------------

One key per file, mode 0644, directory 0755, owned by root:

    # Proskenion package signing anchor (§6.11)
    # key-id: 3f7a1c9e2b4d6085
    # release key, held by Simon
    ed25519 tVJ8QkrN0X5…base64 of the 32 raw public key bytes…=

Lines beginning '#' are comments and blank lines are ignored. There is exactly
one key line; a file with two is rejected. The key is base64 of the 32 raw
Ed25519 public key bytes — not PEM, not OpenSSH, so the verifier cannot be
talked into parsing a certificate or an algorithm it did not ask for.

The key id is DERIVED by the verifier — the first eight bytes of the SHA-256
of the raw key, as hex — and the '# key-id:' line is documentation. A comment
that disagrees with its key is logged and ignored, never believed.

A *.pub that is not a regular file, a symlink above all, is ignored: an anchor
must be the file the root image put here, not a pointer to somewhere writable.

Installing the real key
-----------------------

The private key is generated and held OFF this machine, and never enters the
repository or continuous integration (§14.1, §22.8):

    uv run python tools/package.py keygen --name release-2026 \
        --out-dir ~/keys --comment "release key, held by Simon"

That writes ~/keys/release-2026.key (PKCS#8 PEM, mode 0600 — back this up in
the password manager and one offline copy) and ~/keys/release-2026.pub.

Copy only the .pub here:

    cp ~/keys/release-2026.pub appliance/share/auditorium/trusted-keys/

and rebuild the image (appliance/image/build.sh), which installs it to
/usr/local/share/auditorium/trusted-keys/ with mode 0644.

Until at least one *.pub is present here, build.sh warns and the appliance
refuses every package with "No package signing key is installed".

System images are different
---------------------------

A system image (§13.6, Q13) is signed by a key this machine generates on first
boot and is verified against /srv/appliance/image-keys/ — never this
directory — so that only images this machine captured restore here. The two
directories are never interchangeable; see docs/build/packages.md §1.
